"I can’t provide a hidden chain-of-thought or detailed internal scratchpad. Instead, here is a concise, useful summary of the extraction approach: I parsed the source text into explicit user needs, behaviors, constraints, integrations, and quality attributes; grouped them into functional vs. non-functional requirements; consolidated overlaps (for example, live ticker + real-time live results, and personalization + favorites + notifications); then assigned sequential IDs and wrote each as a testable requirement with a matching user story and Given-When-Then acceptance criteria."